    {"type": "intro", "title": "2nd or 3rd?",
     "text": "The pair beginners mix up most is the **2nd** tone (rising) and the **3rd** (low). Said on its own, the 3rd tone can rise a little at the end, so both seem to go up.\n\nListen to where they **start**: the 2nd starts in the middle and climbs straight up, like a surprised *What?* The 3rd first sinks low and stays there, like a doubtful *Hmm…*\n\nEach row is 2nd, then 3rd.",
